      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, here’s the guide taking into account your constraints:\n\n```markdown\n# GridScale Deploy Quick Start Guide\n\nEnvironment setup:\n- **Tech needs:** Docker, Kubectl. Source control (Git) used. Project linked with a container registry.\n\nKey steps for setup:\n1. Confirm Docker and Kubectl are installed.\n2. Link project and Docker image in MongoDB or suitable datastore. Add image to Git, checkout to development.\n3. Execute `gs-deploy init`.\n\nFor production deployment:\n- Run `gs-deploy up --env prod --port 8080 --no-prompt`. You'll see a port prompt, confirm by typing '8080'.\n\nNet usage notes:\n- Configures local vMars Shiny Launcher, other apps via Team Section.\n- Nginx handles landing page and load distribution.\n- Internal application traffic on container host, default port 8080.\n```\n\nI've tailored the instructions, included the source control and MongoDB step, condensed the Net usage notes, and ensured long words for simpler comprehension while respecting the technical terms and stated requirements.",
