      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Understood, I'll add more information while keeping it concise:\n\n```markdown\n# GridScale Deploy Quick Start Guide - Enhanced\n\n## Environment Setup:\n- **Tech Requirements:** Docker for containerization, Kubectl for Kubernetes cluster interaction. Let's assume you have a Git repository with your project's codebase.\n\n- **Initial Steps:**\n  1. Verify Docker and Kubectl installations with `docker --version` and `kubectl version --client`.\n  2. Link the Docker image from your Git repository to a database like MongoDB, ensuring the image is accessible for GridScale Deploy to use.\n  3. Execute `gs-deploy init` in the project's directory to set up the deployment environment.\n\n## Deployment Overview:\nUpon successful initialization, the following key steps are part of the default deployment lifecycle when executing `gs-deploy up --env prod --port 8080 --no-prompt`:\n\n- **Initialization:** Prepares your local environment, including infrastructure setup.\n- **Deployment:** Launches your application on Kubernetes, scaling to meet demand.\n- **Hot-Reload:** Allows for dynamic updates to the running application without downtime.\n- **Cleanup:** Gracefully terminates instances when no longer needed.\n\n**Port Indices and Traffic Management",
